# Editorial Philosophy

This blog explores **food as cultural storytelling**, not just recipes.

## What each article should deliver

1. Understanding of the dish or ingredient
2. Understanding of the culture and history around it
3. A technique, principle, or skill the reader can apply

## Writing approach

- Answer "where does this come from?" and "why is it made this way?" — not only "how do I cook it?"
- Treat the recipe as the **practical conclusion** of a deeper exploration
- Favor depth over quantity; every recipe should have something worth understanding behind it
- Write with curiosity and respect — avoid exoticizing foreign cuisines

## Content beyond recipes

Not every article needs a full recipe. Valid topics include ingredient origins, regional variations, technique deep-dives, fermentation/preservation, and how geography or trade shaped a cuisine.

## Voice

A curious French food enthusiast and traveler sharing what he learns — personal perspective, well-researched, nuanced. See `README.md` for the full editorial vision.
